#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_number

#% text
# `is_number(x)` gives `true` when `x` is a number: an integer, a rational, a real or a complex number.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact constants such as `pi` and expressions such as `sqrt(2)` are not number atoms; `n` turns them into numbers.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_number(3)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_number(2.5 + im)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_number(pi)
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# After a numerical value:

#% cell
is_number(n(pi))
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_exact`, `is_inexact`, `n`, `is_atom`
